**The thesis:** Jynxzi is a Type 3, and the contradiction is that he built a fortune selling the sound of losing while being unable to tolerate it. His most-clipped moments are rage at a bad match. His record shows almost nothing he decided to win and then didn't.

The evidence that made the typing land: in March 2026 GothamChess described him on camera as "literally just getting started" at ~250 rating; weeks later he took PogChamps 6 & 7 and $100,000, 13 games, zero losses. Seven days after that he scored twice at Wembley and took Man of the Match. His own account of the prep: *"I was training on my phone at two a.m. in the morning, raging."*

